# Project Rules

- Before doing anything, read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. It is authoritative.
- Always identify which agent persona you are acting as (see `.cursor/agents/`)
  before starting work, and stay inside that agent's scope.
- Follow the matching workflow in `.cursor/workflows/` step by step. Do not
  skip or reorder steps. For large projects, `version-workflow.md` is the
  top-level loop — see `.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc`.
- Prefer the Graphify knowledge graph over reading/grepping raw files when
  exploring the codebase — see `.cursor/rules/graphify.mdc`.
- Never modify `AGENTS.md`, files in `.cursor/rules/`, or files in
  `.cursor/workflows/` unless the human explicitly asks for it.
- If a requirement is ambiguous, stop and ask a clarifying question instead
  of guessing.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs over large rewrites.
- Every change must be explainable in one or two sentences in the commit
  message / PR description.
